kai_gazebo ships worlds built on site models made from open data:

- Sydney International Regatta Centre, Nathan Benderson Park, Sand Island
  and La Spezia: each site and its optional seabed are models on Gazebo
  Fuel (https://app.gazebosim.org/honurobotics: sydney_regatta,
  sydney_regatta_seabed, benderson_park, benderson_park_seabed,
  sand_island, sand_island_seabed, la_spezia and la_spezia_seabed),
  fetched at run time, and their water (models/water_surface_sydney_regatta,
  water_surface_benderson_park, water_surface_sand_island and
  water_surface_la_spezia) ships here, all by Honu Robotics under the
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. They are built
  from:
  - OpenStreetMap: the shoreline, land cover, buildings, bridges, piers,
    breakwaters, cranes, trees and seamarks. Map data (c) OpenStreetMap
    contributors, available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0,
    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. The meshes are a Produced Work
    of that data.
  - Sentinel-2 cloudless (https://s2maps.eu) by EOX IT Services GmbH
    (contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2016), under the Creative
    Commons Attribution 4.0 International License: the colour of the ground
    and of the far field in the skies.
  - The AWS Terrain Tiles (https://registry.opendata.aws/terrain-tiles/),
    Mapzen's Terrarium elevation: SRTM, USGS 3DEP and NED, GMTED2010, ETOPO1
    and others, see https://github.com/tilezen/joerd/blob/master/docs/attribution.md.
  - Poly Haven skies (https://polyhaven.com), CC0: rustig_koppie_puresky at
    Sydney Regatta, farm_field_puresky at Benderson Park, sunflowers_puresky at Sand Island and
    kloofendal_38d_partly_cloudy_puresky at La Spezia, turned and with the
    far field painted in.
  - Sydney Regatta's and Benderson Park's seabeds: modelled, as no survey
    of the lakes is open; flat at the depths the venues publish (5 m, NSW
    Office of Sport; at least 3.5 m, dredged to FISA's depth), sloping up
    to the banks. Plausible, not surveyed.
  - Sand Island's seabed: NOAA NCEI's Continuously Updated Digital
    Elevation Model (CUDEM), 1/9 arc second topobathymetric tiles, Hawaii
    (2021), https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/products/coastal-elevation-models, a
    work of the US Government, in the public domain.
  - La Spezia's seabed: Regione Liguria's detailed isobaths (Piano di
    Tutela dell'Ambiente Marino e Costiero, multibeam surveys 2010 to 2019),
    https://geoportal.regione.liguria.it, under the Creative Commons
    Attribution 4.0 International License; elsewhere in the gulf and the
    port the bed is modelled from published depths (the Port Regulatory
    Plan of La Spezia, the Port Authority of the Eastern Ligurian Sea,
    marina guides). Plausible, not surveyed: not for navigation.
- Marina Bay, Singapore: the site, the Singapore Flyer's wheel and the
  optional seabed are models on Gazebo Fuel
  (https://app.gazebosim.org/honurobotics: marina_bay, marina_bay_flyer and
  marina_bay_seabed), fetched at run time, and its water
  (models/water_surface_day) ships here, all by Honu Robotics under the
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License. They are built
  from:
  - OpenStreetMap: the shoreline, land cover, buildings, bridges and trees.
    Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open
    Database License (ODbL) 1.0, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright.
    The meshes are a Produced Work of that data.
  - The organisers' published site plan: the RobotX pontoon and course
    positions.
  - Poly Haven's kloofendal_48d_partly_cloudy_puresky
    (https://polyhaven.com), CC0, regraded and cropped.
  - The seabed: modelled, as no survey of Marina Reservoir is open; the
    reservoir at the depths reported for its water sampling sites, about 5
    to 7 m, and the strait south of the barrage from GEBCO 2025's general
    depths (https://www.gebco.net, public domain). Plausible, not surveyed:
    not for navigation.
  The textures and the modelled landmarks are procedural.
- The aquatic centre: the hall, its pools and their water, a model on
  Gazebo Fuel (https://app.gazebosim.org/honurobotics: aquatic_centre),
  fetched at run time, by Honu Robotics under the Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International License. It is procedural, except the sky
  outside the glass: Poly Haven's kloofendal_38d_partly_cloudy_puresky
  (https://polyhaven.com), CC0.
